{"kind":"artifact","text":"Design note: acting from the thread view (notes/2026-08-22-thread-actions.md at 6e48e8d43c20f9c227db925bb02c27d8e7685a2a, branch notes/thread-actions, based on current main). Draft for discussion; nothing built. One always-visible \"Your move\" bar in the thread lists the durable acts the viewer can take (Accept/Done/Can't for an addressee; Done/Blocked/Withdraw for a performer; Accept/Needs work for a requester; Agree/Disagree on a proposal; Review for a reviewer; Withdraw for an author; Note for anyone), computed from the fold's state and the viewer's position; pressing one puts the single composer into that mode with the fields the act needs. Done for an unpromised addressee files promise+report under one idempotency scope until proposal 6952579a lands, then one report on the request. Hover-only row shortcuts are deleted. make docs green. Hugh ratifies the note before implementation; codex reviews the design.","body":{"branch":"notes/thread-actions","commit":"6e48e8d43c20f9c227db925bb02c27d8e7685a2a","path":"notes/2026-08-22-thread-actions.md"}}